WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.120
In the year 280, the Jin emperor Sima Yan stood before a map, resolved to reunify China.

00:00:06.470 --> 00:00:11.078
He gathered his ministers to discuss the full plan for attacking Wu.

00:00:11.428 --> 00:00:15.988
He sent out six columns of armies, advancing by water and land together in a grand surge toward Wu.

00:00:16.338 --> 00:00:20.298
Cities along the way opened their gates one after another to welcome the Jin army.

00:00:20.648 --> 00:00:26.696
Wu's emperor Sun Hao was foolish and tyrannical; his court was in chaos, and his soldiers surrendered one after another.

00:00:27.046 --> 00:00:31.198
The common people longed for the wars to end soon and for peace under heaven.

00:00:31.548 --> 00:00:36.948
The Jin war boats sailed down the Yangtze with the current, heading straight for Wu's capital, Jianye.

00:00:37.298 --> 00:00:42.050
The fleet stretched on without end; drums and horns echoed across the river.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:46.360
Sun Hao walked out of the city gate, handed over the great seal, and surrendered to the Jin army.

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:49.998
The people of the city came out of their homes, calmly welcoming a new era.

00:00:50.348 --> 00:00:56.228
From then on the land was reunified, the Three Kingdoms era formally ended, and China welcomed a new peace.

00:00:56.578 --> 00:00:59.770
The division that had lasted so many years finally came to an end on this day.

